the future of european space policy was  up for debate as ministers responsible  for competitiveness in the eu met in  brussels  italian astronaut luca pamitano who  spent four months in the international  space station shared his experiences  with the council as ministers discussed  the challenges of space policy europe is  future  it's to me  it's one and the same word the future is  the evolution of society the the  evolution of our country is evolving  into something else something bigger  something better  but space also talks about future  it is the  the place where future things happen and  are prepared travel closer to earth was  also on the agenda ministers agreed on a  broad outline of reform for the travel  package directive the arrival of online  travel services has changed the way the  sector operates and the eu wants to make  sure that protection for travellers is  kept up to date the agreement means that  negotiations can begin shortly with the  european parliament with the aim of  concluding the reform as soon as  possible in other developments the  council reached an informal agreement on  safety standards the union's looking to  modernize safety requirements for  personal protection equipment and  devices using cables for transport like  cable cars and chair lifts the aims to  strengthen controls without placing a  heavy burden or heavy costs on industry
 

